      ⍝ Bugs28 #12 regression: a dyadic scalar function (here "-") whose
      ⍝ *temporary* left argument came from another scalar function
      ⍝ ("1×3") leaked its own result when a following monadic scalar
      ⍝ function then failed -- Prefix::pop_args_push_result() dropped
      ⍝ the discarded left-argument token without releasing its value,
      ⍝ invisible as long as something else reused that Prefix slot
      ⍝ before the statement ended, but a leak once an exception (here
      ⍝ !'s own DOMAIN ERROR) ended it first.
      ⍝
